recipe('air-fryer-chicken-kiev','Garlic butter chicken Kyiv',C,4,190,25,18,[(600,'chicken','Four 150 g breasts'),(60,'butter','Softened'),(10,'garlic','Grated'),(10,'parsley','Chopped'),(60,'flour'),(100,'egg','Beaten'),(60,'crumbs'),(2,'paprika'),(10,'oil')],['Mash butter with garlic and parsley. Shape into four short logs and freeze for 20 minutes. Cut a pocket into the thick side of each breast, insert a butter log and close firmly with a toothpick. Refrigerate for 15 minutes.','Coat chicken in paprika-seasoned flour, then egg, then breadcrumbs. Press crumbs over each seam and brush with oil.','Air fry at 190°C for 15–18 minutes, turning carefully halfway. Probe the thick chicken wall, not just the hot butter pocket, to confirm 74°C. Rest for 5 minutes, remove toothpicks and cut carefully because the filling is hot.'],'A crisp crumb coating encloses chicken breast and a melting garlic-parsley butter centre.',preheat=3,wait=40,internal=74,allergens=['milk','wheat','gluten','egg'],equipment=['Wooden toothpicks'],nutritionNote='All garlic butter and coating counted, including any that leaks into the basket. Freezing, chilling and resting time included. Source nutrition replaced by exact weighed-ingredient calculation.')
recipe('chicken-katsu-curry','Chicken katsu with carrot curry sauce',C,4,180,20,30,[(600,'chicken','Four 150 g cutlets, flattened to 1 cm'),(60,'flour','50 g for coating; 10 g for sauce'),(50,'egg','Beaten'),(100,'crumbs'),(15,'oil','10 g for coating; 5 g for sauce'),(150,'onion','Diced'),(7,'garlic','Grated'),(7,'ginger','Grated'),(120,'carrot','Finely diced'),[15,'curry powder','F003337'],[500,'prepared vegetable stock','F008936','','prepared'],(10,'soy'),(7,'honey')],['Soften onion and carrot in 5 g oil in a saucepan for 5 minutes. Stir in garlic, ginger and curry powder, then 10 g flour. Gradually whisk in stock; simmer 15 minutes, then blend and add soy and honey.','While the sauce simmers, coat thin chicken cutlets in remaining flour, egg and breadcrumbs. Brush with remaining oil.','Air fry at 180°C for 15–20 minutes, turning halfway, until crisp and 74°C inside. Slice onto plates and spoon hot curry sauce alongside. If cutlets require two batches, allow up to 20 extra minutes.'],'Crisp chicken cutlets sit beside a smooth carrot, ginger and curry sauce.',preheat=3,internal=74,allergens=['wheat','gluten','egg','soy'],equipment=['Saucepan','Stick blender'],nutritionNote='Rice is not included. Olive oil replaces coconut oil. Prepared stock and every measured coating ingredient are included; cooking time assumes chicken and sauce cook concurrently.')
recipe('garlic-butter-lobster-tails','Garlic butter lobster tails',S,2,190,15,8,[[200,'raw lobster meat','F005228','Two thawed tails, 100 g edible meat each; keep lower shells'],(40,'butter','Melted'),(10,'garlic','Grated'),(5,'lemon'),(2,'paprika'),(5,'parsley','Chopped')],['Using kitchen scissors, split the top shell of each tail lengthways, stopping before the tail fan. Lift the meat carefully onto the shell while keeping its base attached; remove any visible intestinal vein.','Mix butter with garlic, lemon, paprika and parsley. Brush half over the exposed meat, keeping the rest in a clean bowl.','Air fry at 190°C for 5–8 minutes until meat is opaque and the thickest part reaches 63°C. Larger tails require extra time. Spoon the clean reserved butter over the hot tails and discard shells when eating.'],'Lobster tails cook in their shells with a small garlic, lemon and paprika butter dressing.',preheat=3,internal=63,allergens=['crustacean','milk'],equipment=['Kitchen scissors'],nutritionNote='Nutrition is based on 200 g edible raw lobster meat, not shell-on purchase weight. All 40 g butter included. Source is NOAA-hosted and credits Seafood Nutrition Partnership.')
recipe('air-fried-teriyaki-bacon-wrapped-dates','Sticky soy bacon-wrapped dates',M,4,200,20,10,[[180,'pitted dried dates','F003496','Twelve large dates'],(120,'bacon','Six thin rashers cut in half'),(10,'soy'),(10,'honey'),(5,'ginger','Grated'),(5,'oil')],['Wrap each date with half a bacon rasher and secure with a soaked toothpick. Mix soy, honey and ginger, then brush a thin layer over each parcel.','Brush the basket lightly with oil and arrange dates with space between them. Air fry at 200°C for 9–10 minutes, turning halfway, until bacon is cooked and reaches 71°C.','Rest for 5 minutes because the date centres are very hot. Remove toothpicks and serve three pieces per person.'],'Sweet dates and salty bacon form warm bite-sized parcels with a light ginger-soy glaze.',wait=35,allergens=['soy','wheat','gluten'],equipment=['Wooden toothpicks, soaked for 30 minutes'],nutritionNote='Measured soy, honey and ginger replace branded miso-teriyaki sauce. Twelve bites make four snack portions; all bacon and glaze counted. Toothpick soaking and cooling included.')
recipe('air-fryer-buffalo-chicken-livers-with-blue-cheese-dipping-sauce','Crumb-free chicken livers with blue cheese yoghurt',C,4,200,20,20,[[450,'raw chicken livers','F002709','Trimmed and patted dry'],(60,'flour'),(2,'paprika'),(1,'chilli'),(5,'garlic','Grated'),(10,'oil'),(20,'butter'),[20,'Tabasco-style pepper sauce','F008077'],[40,'blue cheese','F002405','Crumbled'],(100,'yoghurt')],['Mix flour with paprika and chilli. Coat dry liver pieces lightly and brush with oil. Keep raw liver and its utensils separate from ready-to-eat food.','Air fry at 200°C in two uncrowded batches for 8–10 minutes each, turning halfway. Check several thick pieces reach 74°C throughout; liver must not remain pink inside.','Melt butter with pepper sauce and garlic in a small saucepan until bubbling; toss with cooked livers. Mix blue cheese with yoghurt in a clean bowl and serve as a dip.'],'A light seasoned flour coating surrounds fully cooked chicken livers, served with a tangy blue cheese yoghurt dip.',internal=74,allergens=['wheat','gluten','milk'],equipment=['Small saucepan'],nutritionNote='Omits the source milk soak and replaces bottled dressing with measured yoghurt and blue cheese. Butter reduced to 20 g from source 227 g; nutrition is recalculated, not copied. Two batches included.')
